<title>AUSTRALIA: Bulk coal carrier aground in Torres Strait.</title>
<headline>Bulk coal carrier aground in Torres Strait.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-07-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Bombay-registered bulk carrier laden with coal has run aground west of Ince Point in the Torres Strait, between Australia and Papua New Guinea, Queensland Transport said in a statement.</p>
<p>Queensland Transport Maritime spokesman John Watkinson said in a statement the vessel, Dakshineshwar, was enroute from Hay Point in India when it ran aground on a sand embankment off Wednesday Island late on Saturday night.</p>
<p>Watkinson said there appeared to be no imminent danger to the local environment, including no threat of an oil spill.</p>
</text>
